  "findings": [
    "groupby_mean_float64 has no operation-level thread scaling in this fixture; the prior 19.486x worker result does not reproduce on trj, where the 16-cell ratio range is 3.168x to 4.341x",
    "df_abs compounds the incumbent advantage at 10M from 1.433x at one thread to 3.537x at the 128-thread cpuset while using only 10 workers",
    "join_inner is already decisive at 1M, peaking at 8.169x with a four-CPU same-L3 cpuset, but high-cap placement erases much of the advantage",
    "sort_values_single at 10M is 0.769x at one thread, 1.002x and NULL_UNDECIDABLE at two, peaks at a 1.332x ratio under the 64-CPU cap, and falls to a decidable 0.921x loss under the 128-thread cpuset",
    "No tested operation used more than 10 workers; requested affinity alone would have materially overstated real parallelism"
  ],
